"view.synastry.help.input" = "This screen lets you calculate 6 different synastry techniques:\n\n- A visual comparison of the charts.\n- The Composite.\n- The Combine (Davison Chart).\n- An aspect comparison.\n- A midpoint comparison.\n- A declination comparison.\n\nYou need to select two charts - or more if you want to calculate a Composite or Combine. You can choose from charts you have already opened in this session. These are listed under 'Charts available in this session' and you select them by clicking on them. You can also search for other charts via 'Search chart'. Type part of the name and click 'Search'. In the results, select the desired chart by clicking on it. You can remove a selected chart again by clicking the circled cross behind its name.\n\nOnce you have selected two charts, you can choose one of the methods via the buttons at the bottom of the screen. If you have selected more than two charts, you can only choose Composite or Combine.\n\nClick the desired button to see the result in the right-hand part of the screen.\n\nIf you change the selected charts after a result has been shown, the results screen is cleared automatically.";
"view.synastry.help.compare" = "Here you see the chart of one of the partners, with the positions of the other partner in the outer circle. You can swap which partner appears in the figure and which appears in the outer circle using the two circled arrows between the two names.\n\nYou can display the chart in black-and-white or color, with or without aspects, and you can export the drawing using the icons above it.";
"view.synastry.help.composite" = "You can choose between two forms of the composite: a calculation using midpoints only, including for the cusps, or a calculation using a reference location. In the latter case, you enter the location and Enigma calculates the midpoint of both MCs and the corresponding cusps for that MC at that location.\n\nKeep in mind that a composite chart can contain configurations that are astronomically impossible - for example, Sun opposite Venus.";
"view.synastry.help.combine" = "Here you have four options: Simplified, Original, Reference location and Spherical midpoint.\n\nThe simplified chart calculates the midpoint in time and, for the location, uses the average longitude and the average latitude.\n\nThe Original variant calculates the midpoint of both MCs and the corresponding cusps, and is otherwise identical to the simplified method.\n\nIf you choose Reference location, Enigma asks for the location and calculates the midpoint of both MCs and the corresponding cusps for that MC at that location.\n\nWith Spherical midpoint, you calculate the true midpoint in location, taking into account that the earth is a sphere.\n\nSee the factsheet for more information.";
"view.synastry.help.aspectcomparison" = "Here you see the aspects between the factors of both partners. There are two lists, one for each partner. The aspects in both lists are the same but grouped differently.\n\nYou can export the results to PDF.";
"view.synastry.help.midpointcomparison" = "This screen shows the midpoints graphically and as a table, separately for both partners. You can indicate whether you want to show the midpoints in the 360-degree dial or in the 90- or 45-degree dial.\n\nIn the tables - a separate table for each partner - you see the factors for both partners, Partner 1 and Partner 2, the midpoint formed, and the factor in the radix of the partner concerned.\n\nYou can export the results to PDF.";
"view.synastry.help.declinationcomparison" = "Here you see, for both partners, a table with parallels and contra-parallels and the orb. The content of both tables is the same but ordered differently.\n\nYou can export the results to PDF.";
